			<h1>Mojeek Search Engine</h1>
			<p class="intro">The truly independent search engine with its own web crawler and index.</p>

			<nav class="toc">
				<h2>Contents</h2>
				<ol>
					<li><a href="#what-is">What is Mojeek?</a></li>
					<li><a href="#independence">Why Independence Matters</a></li>
					<li><a href="#privacy">Privacy Features</a></li>
					<li><a href="#search-quality">Search Quality</a></li>
					<li><a href="#features">Unique Features</a></li>
					<li><a href="#pros-cons">Pros and Cons</a></li>
					<li><a href="#setup">How to Use Mojeek</a></li>
					<li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<section id="what-is">
				<h2>What is Mojeek?</h2>
				<p>Mojeek is a UK-based search engine that stands out for one key reason: it has its own independently built search index. While most "alternative" search engines actually get their results from Google or Bing, Mojeek crawls the web itself.</p>

				<div class="highlight-box">
					<h3>Quick Facts</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Founded:</strong> 2004 (UK)</li>
						<li><strong>Index:</strong> Own (8+ billion pages)</li>
						<li><strong>AI Features:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Tracking:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Unique:</strong> Fully independent index</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<h3>What Makes Mojeek Different</h3>
				<div class="comparison-table">
					<div class="table-wrapper">
						<table>
							<thead>
								<tr>
									<th>Search Engine</th>
									<th>Index Source</th>
								</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								<tr>
									<td><strong>Mojeek</strong></td>
									<td class="status-good">Own independent index</td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td>DuckDuckGo</td>
									<td>Bing</td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td>Startpage</td>
									<td>Google</td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td>Ecosia</td>
									<td>Bing</td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td>Qwant</td>
									<td>Own + Bing</td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td>Brave Search</td>
									<td>Own independent index</td>
								</tr>
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="independence">
				<h2>Why Independence Matters</h2>

				<p>When a search engine uses Google or Bing's index, several issues arise:</p>

				<div class="feature-grid">
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Dependency</h3>
						<p>If Google or Bing changes their algorithms or policies, dependent search engines are affected.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Same Biases</h3>
						<p>Results inherit the biases and filtering of the underlying index.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Data Sharing</h3>
						<p>Queries are sent to Google or Bing (even if anonymized).</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Limited Control</h3>
						<p>No control over ranking algorithms or what gets indexed.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h3>Mojeek's Approach</h3>
				<p>Mojeek solves these problems by:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Operating its own crawler</strong> - MojeekBot visits websites directly</li>
					<li><strong>Building its own index</strong> - Over 8 billion pages indexed</li>
					<li><strong>Developing its own ranking</strong> - Transparent ranking algorithm</li>
					<li><strong>No external dependencies</strong> - Fully self-contained</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="privacy">
				<h2>Privacy Features</h2>

				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">No Tracking</span>
							<span class="engine-tag green">No Profiling</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<h3>What Mojeek Doesn't Collect</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>IP addresses</li>
						<li>Search history</li>
						<li>User profiles</li>
						<li>Tracking cookies</li>
						<li>Browser fingerprints</li>
						<li>Any personal data</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Privacy Policy Highlights</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>No tracking at all</strong> - Not even anonymized tracking</li>
						<li><strong>No data sales</strong> - Never sells user data</li>
						<li><strong>Minimal logging</strong> - Only aggregate statistics</li>
						<li><strong>UK-based</strong> - Subject to UK/EU privacy laws</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Verification</h3>
					<p>Mojeek's privacy claims are verifiable - they don't set cookies and don't store IP addresses. You can check this yourself in your browser's developer tools.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="search-quality">
				<h2>Search Quality</h2>

				<h3>The Trade-Off</h3>
				<p>Mojeek's independent index is both its strength and limitation:</p>

				<div class="pros-cons">
					<div class="pros">
						<h4>Strengths</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>No filter bubbles</li>
							<li>Unbiased results</li>
							<li>Same for everyone</li>
							<li>Transparent ranking</li>
							<li>No SEO manipulation</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="cons">
						<h4>Limitations</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Smaller index than Google</li>
							<li>May miss niche content</li>
							<li>Less comprehensive for some queries</li>
							<li>Fewer instant answers</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h3>When Mojeek Works Well</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>General searches</strong> - Everyday queries work fine</li>
					<li><strong>Discovering new content</strong> - Results differ from Google</li>
					<li><strong>Avoiding SEO spam</strong> - Less manipulation in results</li>
					<li><strong>Research</strong> - Find content Google might bury</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>When You Might Need Another Engine</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Very specific technical queries</li>
					<li>Recent news (smaller news index)</li>
					<li>Local business searches</li>
					<li>Image search (limited)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="features">
				<h2>Unique Features</h2>

				<div class="feature-grid">
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Emotion Filters</h3>
						<p>Filter results by emotional tone (informational, opinion, commercial). Unique to Mojeek.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Focus Search</h3>
						<p>Narrow results to specific topics like news, blogs, or specific site types.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>No Personalization</h3>
						<p>Everyone sees the same results. No filter bubbles based on past behavior.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Transparent Ranking</h3>
						<p>Mojeek explains how their ranking works - unusual transparency for a search engine.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h3>Summary Feature</h3>
				<p>Mojeek has an optional "Summarize" feature for search results, but it's:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Manual and opt-in (not automatic)</li>
					<li>You click a button to request a summary</li>
					<li>Not forced on every search like Google's AI Overview</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="pros-cons">
				<h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

				<div class="pros-cons">
					<div class="pros">
						<h4>Pros</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Truly independent index</li>
							<li>Zero tracking</li>
							<li>No filter bubbles</li>
							<li>Transparent operations</li>
							<li>No AI forced on you</li>
							<li>Unique emotion filters</li>
							<li>UK-based (strong privacy laws)</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="cons">
						<h4>Cons</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Smaller index than Google</li>
							<li>Some queries less comprehensive</li>
							<li>Limited image search</li>
							<li>Fewer advanced features</li>
							<li>Less refined interface</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="setup">
				<h2>How to Use Mojeek</h2>

				<div class="browser-section">
					<h3>Try It Out</h3>
					<p>Just visit <code>mojeek.com</code> and search. No signup needed.</p>

					<h3>Set as Default Search Engine</h3>
					<p>Use this URL:</p>
					<code class="code-block">https://www.mojeek.com/search?q=%s</code>

					<h3>Browser Instructions</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Search engine → Manage → Add</li>
						<li><strong>Firefox:</strong> Visit mojeek.com, click address bar, add search engine</li>
						<li><strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Privacy → Address bar → Manage → Add</li>
						<li><strong>Safari:</strong> Not available as custom engine</li>
					</ul>

					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine" class="cta-button secondary">Full Setup Guide</a>
				</div>

				<div class="browser-section" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
					<h3>Customize Your Experience</h3>
					<p>Mojeek offers settings (saved without cookies) for:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Safe search level</li>
						<li>Results per page</li>
						<li>Date filtering</li>
						<li>Region preferences</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="faq">
				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is Mojeek?</h3>
					<p>Mojeek is a UK-based search engine that operates its own web crawler and search index. Unlike most alternatives, it doesn't use Google or Bing for results - it's truly independent with no tracking.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Does Mojeek use Google or Bing?</h3>
					<p>No. Mojeek is one of the few search engines with a completely independent index. It crawls the web with its own bot (MojeekBot) and builds its own index of over 8 billion pages.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Mojeek private?</h3>
					<p>Yes. Mojeek has a strict no-tracking policy - no IP logging, no cookies, no user profiles, no data sales. It's one of the most privacy-focused search engines available.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>How good is Mojeek search quality?</h3>
					<p>Mojeek works well for general searches. Its smaller index means it may miss some niche content that Google would find. Many users appreciate the unfiltered, unbiased results without personalization or SEO manipulation.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Does Mojeek have AI features?</h3>
					<p>Mojeek has an optional summarize feature, but it's manual - you click a button to request it. There are no automatic AI summaries or AI-generated content forced on your search results.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="next-steps">
				<h2>Next Steps</h2>
				<div class="next-links">
					<a href="/guides/best-private-search-engines">
						<span>Compare</span>
						<strong>Best Private Search Engines</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine">
						<span>Setup</span>
						<strong>Set as Default Search</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/presearch-search-engine">
						<span>Alternative</span>
						<strong>Presearch</strong>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>

